    summary_60s: 'Non-communicable diseases (NCDs) are long-term health conditions that cannot spread from person to person. Unlike infections (e.g., malaria or flu), NCDs develop slowly and are often linked to lifestyle, genetics, or environmental factors. Examples of NCDs in Nigeria: Hypertensio',
